run#aCorrectiveRoundIsHandedTheCorrections| change's evidence instead of re-deriving them. The declared case count is `LOOP-MEASURE-SUITE cases=`; the
run#aCorrectiveRoundIsHandedTheCorrections| gate's own timing is `LOOP-MEASURE-GATE seconds=`. Neither is counted again by hand.
run#aCorrectiveRoundIsHandedTheCorrections| 
run#aCorrectiveRoundIsHandedTheCorrections| **A file you have read once is cited, not read again.** When a later step needs a fact from a file already in
run#aCorrectiveRoundIsHandedTheCorrections| your transcript, read the line you have; a second read of the same path is a second model turn and buys
run#aCorrectiveRoundIsHandedTheCorrections| nothing. The same holds for a command: a measurement you have taken is quoted, not re-taken. Measured on five
run#aCorrectiveRoundIsHandedTheCorrections| items of this loop (issue #246): 8 to 49 of every item's 22 to 79 file reads were a second read. Prose did not hold
run#aCorrectiveRoundIsHandedTheCorrections| it: `tools/pi-trim-result.mjs` counts each second read of a path you were handed — `metrics.repeatReads` in the
run#aCorrectiveRoundIsHandedTheCorrections| report — and under `LOOP_REPEAT_READ=refuse` answers it with the earlier result's line range, not the text.
run#aCorrectiveRoundIsHandedTheCorrections| 
