run#aCorrectiveRoundIsHandedTheCorrections| (about 2 000 lines or 50 kB per result, `docs/2026-11-07-reviewer-model-analysis.md`) — so a result that
run#aCorrectiveRoundIsHandedTheCorrections| carries that marker, or that ends before the file's last line, is the file's head and not the file. Page it with
run#aCorrectiveRoundIsHandedTheCorrections| `ctx_read`'s `offset` and `limit` until the last line arrives, and quote, cite or edit only a window that arrived whole
run#aCorrectiveRoundIsHandedTheCorrections| (issue #818).
run#aCorrectiveRoundIsHandedTheCorrections| 
run#aCorrectiveRoundIsHandedTheCorrections| **Independent calls belong in one turn, not in one turn each.** A read, a search, a `git log` and a `jq` that do
run#aCorrectiveRoundIsHandedTheCorrections| not need each other's output are one turn's work: issue them together and read the four answers once. Every turn
run#aCorrectiveRoundIsHandedTheCorrections| re-reads the whole conversation, so the second call of a pair paid a turn costs the item its context again without
run#aCorrectiveRoundIsHandedTheCorrections| buying a fact — measured over this loop's archive (227 items, 2026-11-03): 36 825 tool calls in 33 183 turns,
run#aCorrectiveRoundIsHandedTheCorrections| **1.11 calls per turn**, 78 k tokens per turn and 97 % of the spend charged as cache read, and the run reports the
run#aCorrectiveRoundIsHandedTheCorrections| ratio per item and per run beside the recorded floor `LOOP_ITEM_CALLS_PER_TURN_MIN`, naming an item that falls
run#aCorrectiveRoundIsHandedTheCorrections| below it. A chain of single-call turns is what turns an item into a decision: it is the same budget spent as one
run#aCorrectiveRoundIsHandedTheCorrections| long conversation, and the run's turn bound for this role (`LOOP_CHILD_TURNS_MAX_WORKER`) ends the child that runs
run#aCorrectiveRoundIsHandedTheCorrections| into it. Batch
run#aCorrectiveRoundIsHandedTheCorrections| the lookups, and split a phase at its first gate (`tools/loop/phase.sh`) rather than carrying one session past it.
